{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"bceaf1d858ef2090","name":"card_event_retaliation","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Germany/Allegiance/events/card_event_retaliation","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"RETALIATION","text":"After your HQ receives damage, deal equal damage to the enemy HQ.","flavorText":"During WWII combat operations sometimes lacked military or tactical importance but were executed anyway out of vengeance.  Operation Steinbock was a strategic bombing campaign conducted by the Luftwaffe in 1941 and lasted from January to May 1944. The campaign is sometimes referred to as the Baby Blitz as it was performed on a much smaller scale than the Blitz campaign against the UK in 1940-41. The campaign became the last strategic air offensive of the Luftwaffe, and even though they lacked resources, they wanted to conduct revenge for the Allied bombing of German cities, and while doing such, attempt to disrupt Allied preparations for the invasion of France. The campaign had very little effect, and instead the Luftwaffe suffered heavy losses and had very little offensive power remaining when the Allied invasion began in June 1944.","faction":"Germany","type":"gotcha","rarity":"Common","cost":2,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_retaliation","title":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_event_retaliation_title","SourceString":"RETALIATION","LocalizedString":"RETALIATION"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::gotcha","faction":"EFactionEnum::Germany","kredits":2,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_event_retaliation_text","SourceString":"After your HQ receives damage, deal equal damage to the enemy HQ.","LocalizedString":"After your HQ receives damage, deal equal damage to the enemy HQ."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_event_retaliation_history","SourceString":"During WWII combat operations sometimes lacked military or tactical importance but were executed anyway 